  "statement": "The inversion, A5 and U(1) Ward identities hold for the three theories (1,0), (0,1) and (1,1). The hidden Hessian is block diagonal on 4_3 \u2295 4_5 (no mixing), so no joint hidden Ward relates y_odd to y_even. Named matching recipes (V_hist \u0394\u00b2 and \u0394, F singular-value and Frobenius ratios, canonical hidden sqrt(H_5/H_3), democratic) disagree by a factor 1.61e+05 and are not Ward identities. One-loop Yukawa betas are of the form \u03b2_o \u221d y_o and \u03b2_e \u221d y_e because inversion forbids mixing: both axes are RG-fixed rays in every scheme variant. A mixed fixed ratio exists in some variants ([{'variant': 'equal_weights', 'r_star': 1.0}, {'variant': 'hodge_fermions', 'r_star': 1.1028156701139649}]) but is an extra ray, not uniqueness. The residual dimension remains 2. No unique ray is forced, so the one-loop / EM / ARF pipeline is not run."
